id: pm-vcs-7ydb
title: selfhost.bundle crossed GitHub's 50 MiB per-file warning and keeps growing with history toward the 100 MiB per-file limit
description: "Measured on the 2026-10-12 close-out branch (pm-vcs#101): selfhost.bundle grew from 49,260,541 bytes (about 46.98 MiB) at the merge base to 53,183,829 bytes (about 50.72 MiB) at the head, and changed in six of that branch's eight commits. The push emitted GitHub's large-file warning, which appears for any single file over 50 MiB. Each commit that changes the self-hosted source or tracker data regenerates the bundle, so it grows with history. GitHub rejects a single repository file over 100 MiB, so any pull request or release commit that adds or updates selfhost.bundle as a Git file would then be blocked. Release assets have a separate, much larger limit, and the release workflow checks the committed bundle without adding it to its release commit. Options: an incremental or thin bundle against a recorded base; compressing or pruning objects that self-host verification does not need; moving the full bundle to a release asset and committing only its digest; or Git LFS, which would need evaluating against the self-host contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: ci,self-host,size
created_at: "2026-10-12T00:59:40.128Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T10:52:11.352Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-12T10:52:11.331Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-12T10:52:11.331Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "Measure the bundle size per regenerating commit over the last 30 days of main and project one year at that writer cadence (bytes and MiB). The committed self-host artifact then stays well below GitHub's 50 MiB per-file warning over that projection, accept:self-host still proves byte-identity of the committed source, and pushes no longer emit the large-file warning."
resolution: "selfhost.bundle is now a single parentless snapshot of the committed source instead of an appended history: 49,260,541 bytes (46.88 MiB) before, 7,498,503 bytes (7.15 MiB) on main at b722307. accept:self-host still proves tip-tree byte-identity."
expected_result: "Measure the bundle size per regenerating commit over the last 30 days of main and project one year at that writer cadence (bytes and MiB). The committed self-host artifact then stays well below GitHub's 50 MiB per-file warning over that projection, accept:self-host still proves byte-identity of the committed source, and pushes no longer emit the large-file warning."
actual_result: "Measured over the last 30 days of main: 15 regenerations at about 2.22 MiB each under the old design, against 0 by construction now. The residual growth comes from the source itself, about 0.106 MiB/day, and projects to about 46 MiB after one year: below the 50 MiB warning, but with little headroom. That residual source growth (tracker history JSONL dominates) is owned by follow-up pm-vcs-d9m8. Merged with every required check green at its head and no unresolved review thread."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T08:05:27.242Z",claude-hub,"pi-agent (re-applied from the duplicate branch record): Revert proof: with only writeSelfHostBundle behaviourally reverted to the pre-change appending writer (new tests and snapshotIsUnchanged kept), 5 of 58 self-host tests fail: 'replaces the snapshot with a fresh parentless commit when the source tree changes' (parents not empty), 'stays bounded across repeated source changes' (11 commits carried, size grows), 'regenerates a pre-bounding history bundle even when its tip tree matches' (unbounded legacy bundle reused unchanged), 'regenerates rather than reuses a thin bundle that declares prerequisites', and 'regenerates rather than reuses a bundle whose advertised tip is not the snapshot commit'. All 58 pass with the bounded writer. Coverage for scripts/self-host.ts back to 100/100/100/100 (a first draft left one uncovered branch: the ?? [] fallback for a header that omits the prerequisites key, which parseBundle accepts; covered with a test that such a header is a valid bounded snapshot)."
  "2026-10-12T08:05:31.364Z",claude-hub,"pi-agent (re-applied from the duplicate branch record): Measured before/after, bytes and MiB. BEFORE (origin/main HEAD, 2026-10-11): 49,260,541 bytes = 46.88 MiB (49.26 MB decimal); a day earlier 46,172,923 bytes = 44.13 MiB. Growth over the last 30 days of main: 14,240,151 -> 49,260,541 bytes across 15 bundle regenerations = +35,020,390 bytes (33.40 MiB), ~1.11 MiB/day, ~2.22 MiB per regeneration. Linear projection of the old design to one year: ~475.3 MB (~452 MiB); crosses the 50 MiB per-file warning within ~3 days and GitHub's 100 MiB hard rejection in ~48 days (~2026-11-28). AFTER (this branch's HEAD commit): 7,433,859 bytes = 7.08 MiB (7.43 MB decimal), a 6.62x reduction. Growth per regeneration is now zero by construction (the bundle replaces its snapshot instead of accumulating); residual growth is source-driven: the equivalent snapshot bundle grew 4,037,205 -> 7,394,951 bytes over the same window (~0.106 MiB/day, ~39 MiB/yr linear, projected ~46 MiB in one year, still below the 50 MiB warning). Gates: npm run release:check pass (with HOME/GIT_CONFIG isolation for CI identity), bun run release:check pass, coverage 100/100/100/100, node --test test/self-host.test.ts 58/58 pass; accept:self-host passes at the branch HEAD against the committed 7.08 MiB bundle."
  "2026-10-12T08:05:32.057Z",claude-hub,"pi-agent (re-applied from the duplicate branch record): Pull request: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/102 (branch fix/bounded-self-host-artifact, 2 commits). Item work complete: bounded single-snapshot writer implemented and committed with the regenerated 7,443,015-byte bundle, coverage 100/100/100/100, both release:check gates green, revert proof recorded, follow-up item pm-vcs-d9m8 filed for the residual source-driven growth."
